	(text "Q1 + Q2 = Darlington. Q2: S8050 (or BC337), carries ~0.8 A pulses. Q1: 2N3904 (or BC547/S9013/2N2222).\nCheck pinouts: S8050/2N3904/2N2222 = E B C, BC337/BC547 = C B E (flat face, legs down).\nR4: 3-4 ohm, e.g. 2x 2 ohm in series (one 2 ohm if pulses are too shallow; never a single 22 ohm). Keep the R4-Q2-COMMON loop short (~0.8 A pulses).\nC1 AC-couples the drive: a stuck-high GPIO can't hold POWER low.\nD1 resets C1 each pulse. R3 speeds Q2 turn-off. No fuse in this path."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 101.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b975ef6f-4e34-4535-b83d-0f665bd50b09")
	)
	(text "AUX - pull-up like the pad's R66, plus read divider"
